					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/wishun" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1204404); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1204404&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609923883" alt="wishun" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1204404)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/wishun" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1204404); return false;" >wishun</a></span> <span class="odate time_1373374608 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">09 Jul 2013 12:56</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1811662">
									

<p>If a man turns into a murderous wolf-human hybrid once every 28 days it doesn't necessarily follow that he is allergic to silver. Assuming that you have a werewolf of myth without testing could get people killed.</p>
<p>Even in the most clear-cut cases it doesn't necessarily follow that the legend is true. Maybe that broken-winged humanoid constantly weeping blood actually is a formerly divine fallen angel, cast out of a literal heaven by a literal YHWH, or maybe it's just something that wants you to think that. Or maybe it's just a mutant that ancient men found once and made up a story about.</p>
<p>Good science dictates that they not jump to conclusions, no matter how &quot;obvious&quot;, until they have some basis for them.</p>

							</div>

								
					
