					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/azradun" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1416455); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1416455&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609923883" alt="Azradun" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1416455)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/azradun" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1416455); return false;" >Azradun</a></span> <span class="odate time_1373560582 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">11 Jul 2013 16:36</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1813121">
									

<p>Agreed. Anomalous items and SCP objects are alien and uncomprehensible (at least their method of functioning). Applying frameworks forged from our cultural legacy (myths) to them without scientific method will fail. Foundation uses rituals and &quot;magic&quot; only when they are proven to work (like the Montauk procedure).</p>
<p>The &quot;divine fallen angel&quot; is scientifically unfalsifiable, making the myth interpretation only one of the possibilities.</p>

							</div>

								
					
